+# Veterinarian Search Narrowed to Exclude Attribute Filtering
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, leaving owners as the only searchable entity. The row was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey. A request to filter the veterinarian list by Specialty (2026-10-25) falls inside that row as written. The owner decided the row at intake.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-9 as written.** Rejected by the owner: filtering the directory by what it already shows is wanted.
+2. **Drop NG-9 for veterinarians.** Rejected by the owner: free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** (chosen). Free-text veterinarian search stays declined; filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in scope.
+
+## Decision
+
+The owner's decision, quoted from the intake record: "Non-goal NG-9 is narrowed: free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, but filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in."
+
+Search for a pet or a visit stays declined, unchanged. The first capability under the narrowing is `REQ-VET-003`, filtering by Specialty.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- `REQ-VET-003` proceeds without contradicting a Non-Goals row.
+- Free-text veterinarian search stays declined; a request for it reopens NG-9 only on a new owner decision.
+- Whether filtering by veterinarian name counts as attribute filtering or as free-text search stays an open question in the PRD.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the first requirement the narrowing admits.
