+# Specialty Filter Queried at the Database and Left Uncached
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+`REQ-VET-003` narrows both veterinarian list routes to one Specialty named in the address. The name is caller-chosen text. The vet repository's reads are cached in one JCache cache with no size limit and no eviction. The three vendor schemas fold letter case differently, and owner search already returns different results per vendor because of that.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Filter in memory over the cached full list.** No new query. The matching rule and the paging would sit in the controller, which the *Web controller* pattern row forbids.
+2. **Database query, cached like the other vet reads.** Every distinct spelling a caller sends becomes a cache entry in an unbounded cache, so any caller can grow heap without limit.
+3. **Database query, uncached** (chosen). A parameterized repository query matches the whole name with case folded inside the query. Only the unfiltered reads stay cached.
+
+## Decision
+
+The Specialty filter is a parameterized repository query, paged for the directory and unpaged for the machine-readable list. Both sides of the comparison are lower-cased in the query, so H2, MySQL, and PostgreSQL agree without relying on column collation. The filtered queries carry no cache annotation. A blank name is normalized to absent by the controller and takes the cached unfiltered path.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Cache memory stays bounded by the unfiltered reads, whatever names callers send.
+- Each filtered request costs one database round trip, plus a count query for the directory.
+- Matching is vendor-independent, unlike owner search.
+- A later filter on a shown attribute follows the same form: queried, parameterized, uncached.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-VET-003
+
+## References
+
+- [system-design.md § Contracts](../system-design.md#contracts)
+- [system-design.md § Scale and Load](../system-design.md#scale-and-load)
+- [Veterinarian Search Narrowed to Exclude Attribute Filtering](2026-10-25-non-goal-veterinarian-search-narrowed.md)
